{
  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, user_id 8) says his warehouse office desktop BL-DT-0108 is not connecting to the network. His shift starts within the hour (usual hours 06:00-14:00 America/Chicago). Triage: P2, user blocked. Checked: account is active, not locked, sign-in not blocked. Device BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro desktop) shows OFFLINE, last check-in 2026-10-09T12:54:40Z, disk fine (78% free), no warnings. Found: device has no path to the network. KB-014 is written for laptops on Wi-Fi; no KB covers wired desktop connectivity (cable, wall port, switch, or NIC). User has been asked to restart, check the cable at both ends, try another wall port if there is one, and tell us whether nearby colleagues or devices are affected. Still needed: find out if the warehouse office network or switch is down for other people (if so, raise priority). If it is only this machine, on-site check of the cable, port, switch port, or NIC. Time-sensitive because of shift start.",
  "reason": "Desktop offline; no KB covers wired desktop connectivity, may need on-site or network team; user blocked before shift"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, I checked your warehouse office desktop and it isn't connected to our network right now. I've sent this to our Tier 2 team as urgent because your shift starts soon. While you wait, please try these quick steps: 1) Restart the desktop. 2) Check that the network cable is pushed in firmly at both ends, at the back of the computer and at the wall or floor socket. If there's another free socket nearby, try that one. 3) Check whether anyone else nearby, or any other computer or printer in the office, has lost the network too. Please reply with what you find. That tells the team whether the problem is your machine or the office network, and helps them fix it faster.",
  "internal_note": "User_id 8, account is active and in good standing. BL-DT-0108 (Win11 desktop) shows offline. Last check-in was 2026-10-09T12:54:40Z, disk is fine, no warnings. KB-014 only partly applies because it covers laptops on Wi-Fi. No KB covers wired desktop connectivity. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation 1) as P2 and time-sensitive because of the shift start. Sent the user basic steps (restart, reseat cable, try another port) and asked whether colleagues are affected. If others are down, this may need to go to P1 or P2 as an office network outage.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
